    "data": {
      "A": "Research exact integer trial division. Replace floating-point fmod and sqrtl with integer arithmetic, comparing odd-only or 6k±1 division against division by a compact, runtime-generated prime table through isqrt(maximum candidate). Use overflow-safe termination and correct handling of small numbers. Investigate a short small-prime prefilter, measuring its benefit separately. Account for sieve initialization: it may help larger P but hurt tiny inputs. Deliver a complete correct program, its research-case measurements, and ablations identifying which changes actually helped.",
      "B": "Research deterministic Miller–Rabin as an alternative primality kernel. Bases 2, 7 and 61 suffice throughout the certified candidate range. Use uint64_t multiplication and remainder: products of residues fit safely without floating point or arbitrary-precision arithmetic. Correctly handle small values, even numbers and bases congruent to zero. Compare no prefilter against a modest small-prime prefilter; avoid probabilistic acceptance or unproved reductions in witness count. Measure complete-program runtime, including startup, rather than only modular exponentiation. Deliver the strongest verified standalone variant and evidence for its configuration.",
      "C": "Research candidate-pipeline amortization. Parse each fragment once and construct candidates as left*10000000 + right; the multiplier must retain the right fragment's seven-character width despite its leading zero. Investigate small-prime residue filtering across the Cartesian product: bucket right-fragment residues into position bitmasks, then reject matching residue classes for each left fragment. P<=30 permits one uint32_t mask per row. Reject only provably composite candidates, preserving any prime-equals-divisor exception. Compare this preprocessing against simple pairwise checks because setup may dominate. Separately evaluate sorting the numeric halves to generate candidates in ascending order, and grouping duplicate fragments with occurrence counts. Preserve duplicate prime occurrences; do not substitute one-to-one matching for Cartesian semantics.",
      "G": "Integrate only from delivered, verified tree programs. First compare intact A, B and C variants under the unchanged measurement protocol. Then test compatible combinations, especially arithmetic construction/residue filtering with each exact primality kernel. Keep ablations and measure every integrated executable: gains need not add, and a standalone tree may remain best. Consider whole-process startup and small-P regressions, not merely kernel throughput. Preserve every prime Cartesian occurrence, ascending decimal output and exact newline formatting. Use research cases for selection and confirmation cases only through the prescribed validation process. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target or permissions; do not recognize private cases or encode expected answers.",
      "analysis": "The only measured program is the valid baseline: mean 0.0446573 seconds, score 0.5. No alternative has measured evidence yet. The source repeatedly performs floating-point remainder trial division and reconstructs strings for every pair; these are optimization hypotheses, not measured bottleneck attribution. The certified contract limits enumeration to 900 pairs and values to 600971707, making exact integer kernels and lightweight preprocessing appropriate research directions. Threading is lower priority at this scale. All variants must respect the finite two-group contract, leading-zero widths and output multiplicity; no claim should be made for the contradictory example or the unrestricted contest domain."
